 "title": "Article 11 | SAMA Rulebook",
 "text": "Skip to main content\nCareers\nContact Us\nSitemap\nHome\nAbout SAMA\nMedia Center\nSupervision\nStatistics\nPublications\nMonetary Policy\nCurrency\nPayment Systems\nE-Services\nHome\nAbout SAMA\nOverview\nOverview\nOur History\nSaudi Central Bank Law\nSaudi Central Bank Functions\nSaudi Central Bank Strategy\nOrganizational Structure\nSaudi Central Bank Management\nMembers of the Board of Directors of the Saudi Central Bank\nSaudi Central Bank Leadership\nOther\nInternational Relations\nMemoranda of Understanding\nRelevant Links\nMedia Center\nNews\nNews\nSpeeches\nSupervision\nRulebook\nLicenses and Permits\nLicensed Entities\nThe Regulatory Sandbox\nOverview\nPermitted Fintechs\nGuidebook\nJoin the Regulatory Sandbox​\nHolidays and Working Hours\nStatistics\nStatistics\nSaudi Central Bank Portal For Open Data\nMonthly Statistics\nPublication Timeline\nEconomic Indicators\nWeekly Money Supply\nWeekly Points of Sale Transactions\nReserve Assets\nData Template on International Reserves and Foreign Currency Liquidity\nSaudi Central Bank survey\nPublications\nEconomic Reports\nAnnual Report\nInflation Report\nKey Economic Developments Report\nEconomic Research\nWorking Papers\nJoint Research Program\nFinancial Reports\nFinancial Stability Report\nFinance Sector Performance Report\nAnnual Financial Report\nOther Reports\nNational Payments Usage Study Report\nMonetary Policy\nMonetary Policy Tools\nRepo Rate\nReverse Repo Rate\nReserve Requirement on Demand Deposits\nReserve Requirement on Saving Deposits\nMonetary Operations\nOpen Market Operations\nThe Weekly Average of Repo and Reverse Repo\nCurrency\nSaudi Currency History\nOverview\nSecurity Features\nSecurity Features for Fifth Issue\nSecurity Features for Sixth Issue\nSaudi Currency Issues\nPilgrims’ Receipts\nFirst Issue\nSecond Issue\nThird Issue\nFourth Issue\nFifth Issue\nSixth Issue\nSpecial Issues\nExchange Rates\nMonthly Exchange Rates\nExchange Rate\nCurrency Converter\nSaudi Riyal Symbol\nOverview\nSaudi Riyal Symbol Guidelines\nPayment Systems\nSADAD\nmada\nSarie\nEsal\nE-Services\nMain navigation\nSAMA Rulebook\nView Updates\nSearch\nTerms and conditions\nENTIRE SECTION\n\t\nCUSTOM PRINT\n\t\nPRINT / SAVE AS PDF\nSAMA Rulebook\nLaws and Implementing Regulations\nImplementing Regulation of the Real Estate Finance Law\nChapter Two Real Estate Finance Contract\nArticle 11\nBook traversal links for Article 11\n‹ Article 10\nArticle 12 ›\nArticle 11\nNo: 1229\tDate(g): 20/2/2013 | Date(h): 10/4/1434\t\nStatus: In-Force\n Download Original PDF\n\nThe real estate finance entity shall not extend credit on any form of finance exceeding 70 percent of the value of the dwelling subject of the real estate finance contract. SAMA may change such percentage according to prevailing market conditions.\n\n* According to Circular No. 371000064087 dated 06/06/1437 H, SAMA decided to increase the maximum loan-to-value (LTV) ratio from (70%) to (85%) for real estate finance companies, excluding banks.\n\nAccording to Circular No. 391000048362 dated 27/04/1439 H, SAMA decided to increase the maximum LTV ratio from (85%) to (90%) for the first home of citizens only, while maintaining the LTV ratio at (70%) for banks and (85%) for real estate finance companies for the second and subsequent homes for all beneficiaries.\n\nBook traversal links for Article 11\n‹ Article 10\nArticle 12 ›\nSAMA Rulebook (Soft Launch)\nLaws and Implementing Regulations\nSaudi Central Bank Law\nSaudi Arabian Monetary Law\nBanking Control Law\nImplementation Rules for Banking Control Law\nFinance Companies Control Law\nImplementing Regulation of the Finance Companies Control Law\nReal Estate Finance Law\nImplementing Regulation of the Real Estate Finance Law\nChapter One Definitions and General Provisions\nChapter Two Real Estate Finance Contract\nArticle 8\nArticle 9\nArticle 10\nArticle 11\nArticle 12\nArticle 13\nArticle 14\nArticle 15\nChapter Three Real Estate Refinance Company\nChapter Four Real Estate Housing Finance Subsidized Product\nFinance Lease Law\nImplementing Regulation of the Finance Lease Law\nLaw of Payments and Payment Services\nImplementing Regulations of Payments and Payment Services Law\nCredit Information Law\nImplementing Regulations of Credit Information Law\nAnti-Money Laundering Law\nImplementing Regulation to the Anti-Money Laundering Law\nLaw on Combating the Financing of Terrorism\nImplementing Regulations of the Law of Combating Terrorist Crimes and its Financing\nSystemically Important Financial Institutions\nClose-out Netting and related Collateral Arrangements Regulation\nAll Financial Institutions\nBanking Sector\nFinance Sector\nPayment Systems and Payment Services Providers\nMoney Exchange Sector\nCredit Bureaus\nRegulatory Sandbox\nSAMA Circulars\n.\nImportant Links\nAbout the Saudi Central Bank\nMedia Center\nE-Services\nOpen Data Platform\nCareers\nHelp & Support\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nSitemap\nComplaints\nContact US\nAddress & Contact\nKingdom of Saudi Arabia - Riyadh\n+966 11 463 3000\n+966 11 466 2936 / 466-2966\nBranches\nFollow us on\n\n© 2026 Saudi Central Bank (SAMA). All rights reserved.\n\nBack to top\nBACK TO TOP",
